Z||000000||gt boy||10-20-2001||04:08 PM||||has anyone installed the stainless steel brake lines on their fieros?  <P>if so how much work was it and did you notice a difference?<P>------------------<BR>"it's too bad he had to run out of talent half way through the corner..."||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||10-20-2001||04:26 PM||||No harder than installing replacement rubber lines.  Take off the old line, bolt in the new one.  <P>Difference?  Should notice that the pedal feels a little firmer, but I'm sure you'd get the same feel from brand new rubber lines.  The main advantage of the SS lines is that they look cool and are actually slightly cheaper than the rubber lines.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||10-20-2001||05:31 PM||||Sure, I put on stainless steel brake lines from the Fiero store, $110 after shipping.  I did notice a difference, but that was mostly due to the grand am conversion I did at the same time. They do look a lot better, and I've heard that they are good for better braking and longer lasting than rubber.  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">     <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||10-20-2001||05:51 PM||||i agree.  a very easy thing to do.  i would say, if you can pull a whell off a hub, you can swap the brake lines! <P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
